Title: RECLAIMED
Author: AI Assistant
Format: Fountain

INT. KITCHEN - DAY

TOM (40s) lies motionless on the pristine white tiled floor. 

A FEMALE PARAMEDIC pumps his chest with aggressive, rhythmic CPR. Her face is beaded with sweat. 

Beside her, a YOUNGER PARAMEDIC stands awkwardly, hands thrust deep into his pockets, eyes glued to the floor.

JESSICA (30s) watches from the center of the room. Her expression is a mask of shock. 

The Female Paramedic stops pressing. She sits back on her heels, pauses, and shakes her head. She looks up at Jessica.

FEMALE PARAMEDIC
I'm so sorry. He's gone.

The words echo, distant and muffled. 

Jessica doesn't move. She slowly turns her head toward the kitchen window.

EXT. BACK GARDEN - CONTINUOUS (THROUGH WINDOW)

Outside, GRACIE, a chocolate Labrador, enthusiastically digs a hole in a vegetable patch, kicking up fresh rocket seedlings to bury a large, new bone.

INT. KITCHEN - CONTINUOUS

Jessica stares at the dog. Her voice is barely a whisper.

JESSICA
I was in the back garden... and I didn't hear anything.

Jessica's right hand grips a gold locket resting against her collarbone. She squeezes it. The smooth metal absorbs her body heat.

A sharp surge of energy ripples through her stance. Her posture straightens. 

She looks down at the scene. 

A dark smear of blood coats the corner of the polished stone kitchen bench. 

On the white tiles below, a pool of blood expands around Tom's head.

JESSICA (V.O.)
Tom’s choice. But her responsibility that they remain pristine.

The front door bangs open. THREE POLICE OFFICERS stream into the kitchen, their heavy boots squeaking on the tiles. 

A FEMALE OFFICER immediately steps between Jessica and the body, gently grabbing Jessica's shoulders.

FEMALE OFFICER
Ma'am, let's step outside. Come with me.

EXT. STREET / EMMA'S FRONT PORCH - MOMENTS LATER

The Female Officer guides a numb Jessica out of the house. 

EMMA (30s), the next-door neighbor, runs across the lawn in mismatched clothes, arms wide open. 

Emma takes Jessica by the arm, steering her toward the house next door.

INT. EMMA'S LIVING ROOM - CONTINUOUS

In stark contrast to Jessica's house, this room is a chaotic, colorful mess. Piles of laundry litter the chairs. 

Emma shoves a mountain of clean clothes to the side of a worn fabric sofa.

EMMA
Sit. Down here.

Jessica sits. She deeply inhales the comforting, sunny scent of fresh laundry rising from the cushions.

EMMA (CONT'D)
Tea.

It is a statement, not a question. Emma hurries into the kitchen.

Jessica looks down at the laundry pile next to her. She picks up a small, colorful children's T-shirt and presses it tightly against her chest. Her body aches with physical longing.

JESSICA (V.O.)
No kids for Tom and Jessica. Bringing their noise, mess, and unpredictability.

Emma returns carrying a mismatched plastic tray. On it sits a chipped teapot, a mismatched sugar bowl, a random milk jug, and two colorful mugs.

Jessica stares at the chaotic tea set.

JESSICA (V.O.) (CONT'D)
Tom wouldn’t have a bar of that. He required symmetry. The regimented order of everything in its designated place.

Emma sits beside her, placing a warm, gentle hand on Jessica's back.

The touch breaks the dam. Tears instantly spill down Jessica's cheeks. 

But her face isn't contorted in agony. Her breath hitches in a massive, overwhelming wave of relief.

FLASHBACK:

INT. KITCHEN - HOUR EARLIER (DIFFERENT ANGLE)

Jessica stands over Tom's dead weight on the floor, gasping for breath. Her shoulder muscles bulge and tremble under her sweater.

JESSICA (V.O.)
All those hours at the gym pumping weights paying off. Tom insisted she’d join. Demanding his wife be buff and fit.

With a massive grunt, Jessica hauls Tom's limp, heavy upper body upward. Her arms strain near their sockets as she carefully aligns him with the counter.

She drops him. 

Tom's head strikes the exact corner of the stone bench with a sickening thud, opening an existing wound wider. 

Jessica steps back, breathing heavily. She looks down at his feet. 

One of Tom's running shoes is perfectly tied. The other lace is loose. 

Jessica quickly kneels, unties the second shoelace, and pulls it free.

INT. EMMA'S LIVING ROOM - PRESENT

Jessica sits on the sofa, holding the child's t-shirt, a quiet, knowing smile touching her lips.

JESSICA (V.O.)
What now?

EXT. BACK GARDEN - LATER (DUSK)

Jessica stands alone on her back porch, looking out at the yard. 

A wet bath towel sits in a crumpled, messy heap on the floor inside the open door behind her. Dust motes dance in the fading light.

Out in the yard, the garden is overgrown. 

Gracie the Labrador trots up the porch steps, her paws covered in fresh dirt. She sits next to Jessica, panting happily.

Jessica kneels down, burying her face in the dog's thick fur.

JESSICA (V.O.)
Her life reclaimed. Just her and Gracie. Darling Gracie, her unwitting accessory after the fact... who’d happily buried the evidence.

FADE OUT.
